# openclaw_auth.snippet
#
# Auth directives for the OpenClaw dashboard subdomain.
# This file is imported by the main Caddyfile at `/etc/caddy/openclaw_auth.snippet`.
#
# Default contents (shipped with the repo): a respond handler that returns 503
# with setup instructions. This is effectively a no-op — when OPENCLAW_DOMAIN
# is unset, the parent block uses `disabled.invalid` and Caddy never routes
# any traffic here.
#
# When the user runs `synap openclaw setup-domain`, this file is REPLACED with
# one of two generated variants:
#
#   cp-oauth (managed pods):
#     forward_auth https://api.synap.live {
#         uri /api/auth/me
#         copy_headers X-Authenticated-User
#         @unauthorized status 401
#         handle_response @unauthorized {
#             redir https://synap.live/login?redirect=https://{host}{uri} temporary
#         }
#     }
#
#   basic (self-hosted):
#     basicauth {
#         openclaw <bcrypt-hash>
#     }

respond "OpenClaw dashboard auth not configured. Run: synap openclaw setup-domain" 503
